**1. Analysis & Description of the PDF**

This study introduces Nano-11, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan nanoparticle derived from sweet corn, as a promising vaccine adjuvant. Nano-11, characterized by its 70-80 nm size and positive surface charge, efficiently adsorbs and delivers negatively charged protein antigens to dendritic cells (DCs). It activates DCs by upregulating costimulatory molecules and inducing IL-1β and IL-12p40 secretion. In mice, Nano-11 significantly boosts antigen-specific antibody responses, comparable to or exceeding aluminum hydroxide adjuvants. It induces a mild, transient inflammatory response at the injection site, resolving faster than aluminum, suggesting a favorable safety profile for this cost-effective, plant-derived adjuvant.

